:"cel-pro","nome":"Proto-Celtic","termine":"*grendo-","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*gʰren-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Back-formation from Old Spanish greñon, from Medieval Latin grenniōnem, ultimately from Proto-Celtic *grendo- (“mustache, beard”), from Proto-Indo-European *gʰren- (“facial hair”). Compare Middle Irish grend, Irish greann.","origine_varieta":"la-med"}]}